description:
Design a 3-to-8 decoder circuit with enable control. When the enable signal (ena) is high, the module activates one of the eight output lines based on the 3-bit binary input (data_in), setting the corresponding output to low while all others remain high. If the enable signal is low, all outputs are set to high. This implementation allows for a straightforward mapping of a 3-bit input to a unique low signal on one of the eight outputs, serving to drive additional logic or devices in a digital system.
module top_module(
    input [2:0] data_in,
    input ena,
    output reg [7:0] data_out
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input [2:0] data_in,
    input ena,
    output reg [7:0] data_out
    );always @ (ena or data_in)
begin
if (ena == 1)
case (data_in)
3'b000:
data_out = 8'b11111110;
3'b001:
data_out = 8'b11111101;
3'b010:
data_out = 8'b11111011;
3'b011:
data_out = 8'b11110111;
3'b100:
data_out = 8'b11101111;
3'b101:
data_out = 8'b11011111;
3'b110:
data_out = 8'b10111111;
3'b111:
data_out = 8'b01111111;
endcase
else
data_out = 8'b11111111;
end


endmodule

