Build a 64-bit shift register with synchronous load. The shifter can shift left or right by 1, 8, or 16 bit positions, selected by "amount."

// Signals are defined as below:
// (1) load: Loads shift register with data[63:0] instead of shifting. Active high.
// (2) ena: Chooses whether to shift. Active high. 
// (3) amount: Chooses which direction and how much to shift. 
//     (a) 3'b000: shift left by 1 bit. 
//     (b) 3'b001: shift left by 8 bits. 
//     (c) 3'b010: shift left by 16 bits. 
//     (d) 3'b100: shift right by 1 bit. 
