description:
Design a circuit that counts the number of ones in a 4-bit input (`in`) on each rising edge of the clock (`clk`). The count is stored in a 3-bit output register (`count`), which increments by one for each high bit detected in the input. The circuit uses a temporary register (`prev_count`) to hold the previous count value before updating, ensuring proper synchronization with the clock. This module effectively functions as a one-hot counter for identifying the number of '1' bits in the given input data.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [3:0] in,
  output reg [2:0] count
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [3:0] in,
  output reg [2:0] count
);reg [2:0] prev_count;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  prev_count <= count;
  count <= prev_count;
  if (in[0] == 1) begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end
  if (in[1] == 1) begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end
  if (in[2] == 1) begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end
  if (in[3] == 1) begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end
end

endmodule

