Design a circuit that detects a rising edge on the input signal and uses it to toggle the output state. This is achieved by monitoring the input signal 'in' in conjunction with the clock signal 'clk' and a reset signal. When a rising edge is detected (when 'in' transitions from LOW to HIGH), the output 'out' changes to its opposite logic level. The circuit also includes a reset functionality, ensuring that both the output and the previous input state are initialized to LOW when the reset signal is asserted.
